 "obituary": {
  "narrative": [
   "Every list on this page starts at a courthouse or a data provider. This one starts earlier: the owner has just passed, no probate case exists yet, and no provider list has the home. DataSift began recording obituary-linked homes in December 2025: 289 are flagged in Frederick County so far, about 36 new filings a month.",
   "Of every 1,000 flagged homes, roughly 450 to 580 eventually sell, and investors buy 20 to 30 percent of those sales. Run that through the same doors-per-deal lens as the ranking sheet and obituary pencils out to 22 to 50 doors per deal (call it 34): about 4 to 6 times sharper than working random doors, behind only the sharpest court-record lists.",
   "This is the model's base case, not this county's own sold history yet. The data only started in December 2025, so the earliest filings are just now reaching their selling window; as they age through it (early 2027) the number graduates to this county's real one."
  ],
  "timeline": [
   {
    "stage": "Month 0",
    "what_happens": "The owner passes. The flag turns on when the obituary publishes. No court record exists, no provider list has the home, and neither do your competitors."
   },
   {
    "stage": "Months 1-3",
    "what_happens": "The estate opens. Families typically file probate 30 to 90 days after the passing, once the funeral is behind them and an attorney is engaged."
   },
   {
    "stage": "Months 3-6",
    "what_happens": "The quiet stretch. Creditor windows (90 days in Florida, 4 months in Tennessee, similar elsewhere) and title work run their course. Very few of these homes close this early, and that is normal."
   },
   {
    "stage": "Months 6-12",
    "what_happens": "The first sales. Most states allow selling during administration, and heirs who need cash move first: as-is condition, documented 5 to 7 percent discounts, often off-market. Roughly a quarter of these homes sell inside the first year."
   },
   {
    "stage": "Months 12-24",
    "what_happens": "The main wave. A typical administration settles around month 14, and the sales concentrate here. This is the window the whole cadence builds toward."
   },
   {
    "stage": "Months 24-36",
    "what_happens": "The tail, then the keepers. About half of these homes have sold by year three. The rest stay in the family, and once a home transfers to heirs who keep it, the sale signal fades fast."
   }
  ],
